EVALUATION:

Which model generated the most useful output?
GPT-2s second prompt approach was structured, but FLAN-T5 and Stable Diffusion weren't good, hallucinated, and missed prompt constraints (like FLAN-T5 renaming the bank and Stable Diffusion missing the sunset keyword). Overall, GPT-2 performed the best here.

How did changing prompts affect outputs?
In GPT-2, little adjustments to the sentences beginnings shifted the model behavior. In Stable Diffusion, modifying lighting and architectural goals changed the aesthetic quality, but lighting instructions seem to be too challenging.

Model Limitations and Errors:
Stable Diffusion struggled with rendering text and brand logos correctly. GPT-2 tends to hallucinate and drift off topic, and it tends to do this more when max tokens are set higher.

Real Business Use and Human Review:
I think the outputs cannot be used directly in a real business without human review. A human reviewer is 100% necessary to rewrite generated text, make sure its safe and factually accurate, and correct hallucinations in summaries and responses.


